    <div style="text-align:center"><div class="kicker">Questions, Answered Straight</div><h2 class="section-title" style="margin:0 auto">Frequently asked questions</h2></div>
    <div style="margin-top:30px" id="faqList">
      <div class="faq open"><button>What exactly is a merchant cash advance? <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i></button><div class="ans">A merchant cash advance (MCA) is not a loan. It’s a purchase of a portion of your future sales at a discount. You receive a lump sum now, and we’re repaid as you remit an agreed amount — either a small percentage of daily sales or a fixed daily/weekly amount — until the purchased amount is delivered. Because it’s based on revenue, approval doesn’t hinge on perfect credit or collateral.</div></div>
      <div class="faq"><button>How fast can I actually get funded? <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i></button><div class="ans">Most complete applications receive a decision in 2–4 business hours. Once approved and signed, funding is typically wired the same or next business day. Timelines depend on how quickly bank statements and verification are provided — that’s why calling after you apply speeds everything up.</div></div>
      <div class="faq"><button>Will applying hurt my credit score? <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i></button><div class="ans">No. Checking your options with Quick Funds Capital uses a soft inquiry only and will not affect your credit score. Your credit profile is one factor we review, but revenue and business performance matter more.</div></div>
      <div class="faq"><button>What do I need to apply? <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i></button><div class="ans">Just the 2-minute application on this page and your last 3 months of business bank statements. For larger amounts, we may ask for additional months or a voided check for deposit. No tax returns are needed to pre-qualify.</div></div>
      <div class="faq"><button>How much does it cost? <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i></button><div class="ans">Cost is quoted as a factor rate (for example, 1.25×) so you know the total payback amount up front — no compounding interest and no hidden origination surprises. Your advisor will show you the total cost, the payment amount, and the estimated term before you sign anything. Early payoff discounts are available on many programs.</div></div>
      <div class="faq"><button>Can I get funded if I already have an advance? <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i></button><div class="ans">Often, yes. Many of our clients take a second position or renew after demonstrating strong payment performance. Tell us about your current obligations in the application notes and your advisor will structure options honestly — including telling you if waiting is the better move.</div></div>
      <div class="faq"><button>What can I use the money for? <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i></button><div class="ans">Anything that helps your business: payroll, inventory, equipment, marketing, renovations, expansion, taxes, or bridging a seasonal gap. There are no use restrictions and no receipts to submit.</div></div>
      <div class="faq"><button>What if my revenue dips? <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i></button><div class="ans">If you’re on a percentage-of-sales program, your remittance naturally moves with your revenue — slower weeks mean smaller remittances. On fixed-payment programs, talk to us early if you hit a rough patch; we’d rather restructure than surprise you.</div></div>
      <div class="faq"><button>Do you fund businesses in my state? <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i></button><div class="ans">Yes — Quick Funds Capital serves small businesses in all 50 states plus Washington, DC, entirely by phone and online. That includes California, Texas, Florida, New York, Illinois, Pennsylvania, Ohio, Georgia, North Carolina, Michigan, New Jersey, Virginia, Washington, Arizona, Massachusetts, Tennessee, Indiana, Missouri, Maryland, Wisconsin, Colorado, Minnesota, South Carolina, Alabama, Louisiana, Kentucky, Oregon, Oklahoma, Connecticut, Utah, Iowa, Nevada, Arkansas, Mississippi, Kansas, New Mexico, Nebraska, Idaho, West Virginia, Hawaii, New Hampshire, Maine, Montana, Delaware, South Dakota, North Dakota, Alaska, Vermont, Wyoming and Rhode Island. See our <a href="#service-area" style="color:#007A4D;font-weight:800">nationwide service area</a> below.</div></div>
      <div class="faq"><button>What are the minimum requirements for business funding? <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i></button><div class="ans">At least 6 months in business, $10,000 or more in monthly business revenue, a U.S. business bank account, and a credit score of 500 or higher (all profiles reviewed). No collateral is required and you must not be in active bankruptcy.</div></div>
